      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Moovingo is delighted to present Apartment 73 The Richmond to the market. This bright two-bedroom apartment extends to approximately 54 sq. m. and is set within a secure gated development in the heart of Dublin 7. Fresh, neutral interiors and wood-effect flooring give the apartment a clean and inviting feel, while the generous living space opens to a private balcony overlooking North Brunswick Street.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation begins with an entrance hallway leading to a spacious living and dining room measuring approximately 4.62 m x 6.03 m. A feature fireplace provides a natural focal point, and glazed double doors open directly onto the balcony. The separate kitchen is positioned just off the living area and includes fitted units, an electric hob and oven, fridge/freezer and washing machine.\r\nThere are two well-proportioned bedrooms, both with fitted wardrobes. The main bedroom measures approximately 2.76 m x 3.77 m, while the second bedroom measures approximately 2.49 m x 3.77 m. A tiled shower room with a large shower enclosure, vanity unit and heated towel rail completes the accommodation.\r\n\r\nThe Richmond is an established development with lift access and attractive communal spaces. Residents have use of landscaped courtyards with seating, a hard-surface recreation tennis court and a large communal roof terrace with views across the city.\r\n\r\nWith a practical layout, excellent natural light and a highly convenient city location, Apartment 73 is likely to appeal to first-time buyers, owner-occupiers and investors alike.\r\n\r\nArea Info:\r\n\r\nThe Richmond is located on North Brunswick Street, between Smithfield, Stoneybatter and Grangegorman. The area offers an excellent mix of independent cafés, restaurants, bars and everyday shopping, with Smithfield Square and the Jameson Distillery close by. TU Dublin's Grangegorman campus is approximately an 11-minute walk, while O'Connell Street is around 22 minutes on foot.\r\n\r\nTransport links are excellent. Smithfield Luas stop is approximately 9 minutes' walk away and provides direct Red Line connections towards Heuston Station, Connolly Station, Busáras and the city centre. Broadstone Luas stop and several Dublin Bus routes are also within easy reach.\r\n\r\nFor culture and recreation, residents are close to the Light House Cinema, the National Museum of Ireland at Collins Barracks and the green open space of Phoenix Park. The city centre, Four Courts and the amenities of Capel Street are all readily accessible on foot.\r\n\r\n\r\nDisclaimer: Any intending purchaser(s) shall accept that no statement, description or measurement contained in advertisement or any other document or published by the vendor or by Moovingo, in respect of the premises shall constitute a representation inducing the purchaser(s) to enter into any contract for sale, or any warranty forming part of any such contract for sale. Any such statement, description or measurement, whether in writing or in oral form, given by the vendor, or by Moovingo, are for illustration purposes only and are not to be taken as matters of fact. Any intending purchaser(s) shall satisfy themselves by inspection, survey or otherwise as to the correctness of same. No omission, misstatement, misdescription, incorrect measurement or error of any description, whether given orally or in any written form by the vendor or by Moovingo, shall give rise to any claim for compensation against the vendor or against Moovingo. Any intending purchaser(s) are deemed to fully satisfy themselves in relation to all such matters."
      },
